      "description": "src/sqllens/safety/readonly.py lines 149-158: is_introspection_query catches every Exception around sqlglot.parse_one and returns False (data query). This change makes that result decide whether a catalog DataFrame is withheld (_format.py lines 431, 436), so a non-parse error (RecursionError, an AttributeError/KeyError bug in sqlglot's dialect parser) shows a schema result and lets an introspection success clear an earlier run_sql error (isError false). The INFO log records only the exception type and calls it 'SQL did not parse'. assert_select_only in the same file catches only (ParseError, TokenError). The docstring (lines 143-145) and docs/internal/database-connectors/read-only-safety.md line 73 describe a narrower catch than the code has.",
